+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered with `ToolRegistry` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` on its `ToolDefinition` in `src/types/ai.ts`, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates model-supplied tool input against that schema before the executor runs. Schema rejections resolve with a structured `ToolResponse` so the orchestrator can pass the failure back to the model within the tool loop, while unregistered tool names continue to throw.
+
+## Input validation on execute
+
+- When tool input violates `required`, declared property types, or `enum` constraints, `execute` resolves with a rejection `ToolResponse` naming each failing property path and constraint without invoking the executor and without writing offending property values into the response or logs ([validated by: rejects malformed tool input with a ToolResponse naming the failing path and constraint without invoking the executor or leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- Unregistered tool names still cause `execute` to throw `Unknown tool: <name>` rather than returning a `ToolResponse`.
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled synchronously at `register` time so an uncompilable schema throws immediately and names the tool ([validated by: throws synchronously at register time when a static inputSchema is uncompilable and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L103)).
+- A static tool's compiled validator is reused across subsequent `execute` calls rather than recompiled on each invocation.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition per `execute` call and validates against the schema current at that call rather than a stale validator ([validated by: validates a function-valued ToolDefinitionSource against the schema current at each execute call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L117)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` caches its compiled validator by the resolved `inputSchema` object reference when the schema object has not changed.
+
+## Tool loop recovery
+
+- When a model issues malformed tool input, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` returns the validation rejection `ToolResponse` in the `tool_result` message so the model can retry within `maxToolRounds`, passing valid input through with unlisted properties preserved and without type coercion or schema default injection ([validated by: drives a rejected tool call through chatOrchestrator to a corrected retry without stripping extra properties or applying defaults](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L162)).
